.el .ds Aq '
.TH acc 1  "acc 0.5.4" 
.SH NAME
acc \- acc — change control for software written with coding agents
.SH SYNOPSIS
\fBacc\fR [\fB\-q\fR|\fB\-\-quiet\fR] [\fB\-v\fR|\fB\-\-verbose\fR] [\fB\-\-no\-color\fR] [\fB\-h\fR|\fB\-\-help\fR] [\fB\-V\fR|\fB\-\-version\fR] <\fIsubcommands\fR>
.SH DESCRIPTION
acc — change control for software written with coding agents.
.PP
Records the agent, human operator, reviewers and merger of each pull request, then evaluates
explicit separation\-of\-duty rules (ACC001 to ACC010) deterministically and offline.
Only `scan`, `export`, `pr` and `doctor \-\-online` contact GitHub (and only the collecting commands
read the clock, for the default window, or `git`, to find the repository); `evaluate`, `validate` and `check` never touch the
network or the clock. No LLM is involved, and agent authorship alone is never a finding.
.PP
Exit codes: 0 ok · 1 policy threshold exceeded (check, pr) · 2 usage (or doctor: broken) · 3 invalid input or
manifest · 4 collection incomplete (beats 1) · 5 authentication rejected · 6 API, permission,
rate\-limit or transport failure · 7 unsupported API data.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
\fB\-q\fR, \fB\-\-quiet\fR
Suppress status lines on stderr
.TP
\fB\-v\fR, \fB\-\-verbose\fR
Print extra diagnostics on stderr (resolved policy, format, destination, counts). Never changes stdout
.TP
\fB\-\-no\-color\fR
Never color diagnostics. acc\*(Aqs own output is never colored; this and a non\-empty NO_COLOR environment variable switch off color in help and usage errors too
.TP
\fB\-h\fR, \fB\-\-help\fR
Print help (see a summary with \*(Aq\-h\*(Aq)
.TP
\fB\-V\fR, \fB\-\-version\fR
Print version
.SH SUBCOMMANDS
.TP
acc\-scan(1)
Collect facts from a forge and write an evaluated manifest
.TP
acc\-export(1)
Export normalized events as JSON for offline evaluation
.TP
acc\-evaluate(1)
Evaluate a normalized event export offline
.TP
acc\-validate(1)
Validate a manifest: schema, timeline, references and recomputed contents
.TP
acc\-check(1)
Enforce policy against a manifest, honoring recorded dispositions
.TP
acc\-pr(1)
Collect and evaluate one pull request
.TP
acc\-doctor(1)
Check that this environment is ready to collect: version, token, policy file, repository; with \-\-online, the token, the rate limit and whether a newer acc exists (GET only)
.TP
acc\-completions(1)
Generate shell completions
.TP
acc\-manpage(1)
Generate man pages
.SH VERSION
v0.5.4
